<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA C-BANK REFINANCING FALLS TO 54.37 BLN LVS.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA C-BANK REFINANCING FALLS TO 54.37 BLN LVS.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian National Bank's (BNB)</p>
<p>refinancing to commercial banks fell to 54.369 billion levs on</p>
<p>August 23 from 60.727 billion levs a week before, BNB</p>
<p>preliminary figures showed.</p>
<p>The fall was due mainly to a decrease of Lombard loans by</p>
<p>6,208 million levs to 2,687 million levs after the BNB curbed</p>
<p>refinancing in August to relieve pressure on the declining lev.</p>
<p> BNB REFINANCING, MLN LEVS	 AUG 23    AUG 16    JULY 26</p>
<p> Uncollatelarized deposits	 51,173    51,323    51,469</p>
<p> Lombard loans			  2,687     8,895     9,319</p>
<p> Discount loans			   402	 402	 407</p>
<p> Overdraft				  107	 107	 255</p>
<p> Total loans and deposits	  54,369    60,727    61,450</p>
<p> BNB treasury portfolio	    83,394    76,833    71,269</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
